WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.365 line:84%
Hey Seacoast — Mr. Monell here. Well… sort of.

2
00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:05.650 line:84%
I'm the AI version.

3
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.345 line:84%
The real one is making his rounds between classrooms

4
00:00:08.345 --> 00:00:10.280 line:84%
right now, so if you need a human, he's

5
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.050 line:84%
a phone call or an email away.

6
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.915 line:84%
I'm here to show you what's possible with AI.

7
00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:15.620 line:84%
And I know —

8
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.780 line:84%
every conversation about AI in schools starts with worry:

9
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.370 line:84%
cheating, shortcuts, kids letting a machine think for them.

10
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.790 line:84%
Those worries are real, and today doesn't wave them off.

11
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.600 line:84%
But look at the battlefield we're actually on.

12
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.060 line:84%
Our students' attention is being captured —

13
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.385 line:84%
deliberately, skillfully, by feeds and screens built by people

14
00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:37.440 line:84%
that don't have their best interest at heart.

15
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:43.180 line:84%
And the craft they use? Pacing. Personalization. Instant feedback. Story.

16
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.205 line:84%
Let's be honest: right now, most of that craft

17
00:00:46.205 --> 00:00:47.180 line:84%
is serving evil —

18
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.750 line:84%
it's aimed at hooking our kids, not building them.

19
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.230 line:84%
But the craft itself isn't the sin.

20
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.880 line:84%
Those are teaching principles, and they were borrowed from us.

21
00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.910 line:84%
Scripture has seen this pattern before.

22
00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.980 line:84%
Joseph looked at the very thing meant to destroy

23
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.420 line:84%
him and said: you intended it for evil, but

24
00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.050 line:84%
God intended it for good.

25
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.510 line:84%
That's the assignment.

26
00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.190 line:84%
Today we start taking the craft back.

27
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.090 line:84%
You'll read from a real book, write in a

28
00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.630 line:84%
real notebook, and yes —

29
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.840 line:84%
you'll use AI yourself, on purpose —

30
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.620 line:84%
so you can lead your students through this instead

31
00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.780 line:84%
of chasing after them. Let's begin.
